    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "The average value of a set of numbers is given by the sum of the numbers divided by the number of elements in the set.\n\nGiven the numbers \\(0\\), \\(2z\\), \\(4z\\), \\(8z\\), and \\(16z\\), we first find the sum of these numbers.\n\\[\n0 + 2z + 4z + 8z + 16z = (0 + 2z + 4z + 8z + 16z) = 30z\n\\]\n\nNext, we determine the number of elements in the set. There are 5 elements in the set \\(\\{0, 2z, 4z, 8z, 16z\\}\\).\n\nFinally, the average value is given by the sum divided by the number of elements:\n\\[\n\\text{Average value} = \\frac{\\text{Sum of the numbers}}{\\text{Number of elements}} = \\frac{30z}{5} = 6z\n\\]\n\nThus, the average value of \\(0\\), \\(2z\\), \\(4z\\), \\(8z\\), and \\(16z\\) is \\(\\boxed{6z}\\).",
